  "vo": [
    {
      "id": "N1",
      "text": "Two days after the ice storm, the Eastside is still dark. Mrs. Lan is seventy-one. Her heat is off, and her phone is at twenty-three percent.",
      "start": "0:01.0",
      "end": "0:12.0",
      "window": 11,
      "words": 26,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 10.4,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 142,
      "measuredSeconds": 10.9
    },
    {
      "id": "N2",
      "text": "Help exists: her neighbors raised a fund. But the form is six pages, in English. After the Eaton fire, one LA group took three hundred requests overnight, in comments on Instagram.",
      "start": "0:12.2",
      "end": "0:25.9",
      "window": 13.7,
      "words": 31,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 12.4,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 136,
      "measuredSeconds": 13.5
    },
    {
      "id": "N3",
      "text": "So we built Neighborline: a hotline, not a dashboard. She just says it.",
      "start": "0:26.1",
      "end": "0:32.8",
      "window": 6.7,
      "words": 13,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 5.2,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 116,
      "measuredSeconds": 6.7
    },
    {
      "id": "V1",
      "text": "She left a voice note, in Vietnamese. Watch the clock.",
      "start": "0:43.0",
      "end": "0:47.5",
      "window": 4.5,
      "words": 10,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 4,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 133,
      "measuredSeconds": 4.55
    },
    {
      "id": "V2",
      "text": "She heard it read back in Vietnamese and said yes. The group's own rules, not the AI, set the amount: a hundred and fifty dollars. Two organizers sign.",
      "start": "0:48.1",
      "end": "1:00.6",
      "window": 12.5,
      "words": 28,
      "wpm": 155,
      "estSeconds": 10.84,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 134,
      "measuredSeconds": 12.5
    },
    {
      "id": "V3",
      "text": "Paid, into her Venmo, with a message in Vietnamese. Twenty-two point five seconds to the SUCCESS webhook, on our PayPal stand-in. The approvals came on cue; real neighbors take longer.",
      "start": "1:02.1",
      "end": "1:17.8",
      "window": 15.7,
      "words": 30,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 12,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 115,
      "note": "Starts 0.6 s before the cut to her phone, 1.4 s after SUCCESS is on screen: \"Paid,\" over the three paid phones, the cut in the pause after it.",
      "measuredSeconds": 15.8
    },
    {
      "id": "V5a",
      "text": "Rosa asks for groceries, in Spanish. Same rules, two approvals.",
      "start": "1:18.3",
      "end": "1:24.3",
      "window": 6,
      "words": 10,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 4,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 100,
      "measuredSeconds": 6.15
    },
    {
      "id": "V5b",
      "text": "Her email has no PayPal account yet: unclaimed. She gets claim help in Spanish.",
      "start": "1:28.7",
      "end": "1:35.5",
      "window": 6.8,
      "words": 14,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 5.6,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 124,
      "note": "Starts 1.5 s before UNCLAIMED lands, so the word \"unclaimed\" is spoken just after it is on screen.",
      "measuredSeconds": 6.9
    },
    {
      "id": "V5c",
      "text": "She claims it. Success. Most payout systems stop at unclaimed; this one follows through.",
      "start": "1:35.6",
      "end": "1:42.8",
      "window": 7.2,
      "words": 14,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 5.6,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 117,
      "note": "\"Success.\" is spoken ~0.7 s after SUCCEEDED is on screen.",
      "measuredSeconds": 7.35
    },
    {
      "id": "V6",
      "text": "Someone posing as the organizers, with a Venmo handle one letter off? Approve is disabled on every phone. No money moves.",
      "start": "1:43.0",
      "end": "1:52.5",
      "window": 9.5,
      "words": 21,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 8.4,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 133,
      "measuredSeconds": 9.65
    },
    {
      "id": "V7a",
      "text": "Under the hood: the agents that talk to neighbors have no PayPal tools. One separate approval service holds the Payouts credentials, and it pays only on a record signed with the passkeys of two different organizers.",
      "start": "1:52.9",
      "end": "2:07.7",
      "window": 14.8,
      "words": 36,
      "wpm": 155,
      "estSeconds": 13.94,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 146,
      "note": "Runs over /trust and into the rail push (Shot 10).",
      "measuredSeconds": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "V7c",
      "text": "The batch ID comes from the signed approval, so a double tap can't pay twice. Webhooks are signature-verified, and every payout is reconciled with PayPal.",
      "start": "2:08.3",
      "end": "2:18.4",
      "window": 10.15,
      "words": 25,
      "wpm": 155,
      "estSeconds": 9.68,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 148,
      "note": "Card 1 (batch ID) to the pause after \"can't pay twice\", card 2 (webhooks) from \"Webhooks are signature-verified\".",
      "measuredSeconds": 10.1
    },
    {
      "id": "V10",
      "text": "For agent builders: the same guard ships as an MCP server. An AI agent asking to pay is refused without two humans' signatures. With them, it pays.",
      "start": "2:18.8",
      "end": "2:30.8",
      "window": 12.05,
      "words": 27,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 10.8,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 134,
      "measuredSeconds": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "V8",
      "text": "Donors give with PayPal or Venmo. The public report never names a neighbor, and every number comes from the ledger.",
      "start": "2:31.2",
      "end": "2:40.2",
      "window": 9.05,
      "words": 20,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 8,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 133,
      "measuredSeconds": 9.05
    },
    {
      "id": "V9",
      "text": "That night, one window on the Eastside is warm again. Neighborline is open source. Try the hotline yourself; the link is below. Because the morning after a storm, help should sound like your own language.",
      "start": "2:40.8",
      "end": "2:55.7",
      "window": 14.9,
      "words": 35,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 14,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 141,
      "measuredSeconds": 14.85
    }
  ],
